{"t": 1794108413.3795023, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_or_update_file", "args": {"branch": "eng-91", "content": "def deprecation_headers(sunset_date: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return the deprecation headers for a v1 endpoint.\n\n    See the \"API guidelines\" page in Notion, section \"Deprecation\".\n    ``sunset_date`` must be an HTTP-date (e.g.\n    ``\"Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:28:00 GMT\"``).\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"Deprecation\": \"true\",\n        \"Sunset\": sunset_date,\n        \"Link\": '<https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"',\n    }\n", "message": "ENG-91: add deprecation headers helper", "owner": "acme", "path": "api/headers.py", "repo": "public-api"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794108416.695719, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Implements `api.headers.deprecation_headers(sunset_date)` as described in ENG-91, following the \"API guidelines\" page in Notion (section \"Deprecation\").\n\nThe helper returns the three headers required for deprecated v1 endpoints:\n\n- `Deprecation: true`\n- `Sunset: <HTTP-date>` (caller-supplied `sunset_date`)\n- `Link: <https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"`\n\nCloses ENG-91.", "head": "eng-91", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api", "title": "ENG-91: Add deprecation headers to v1 endpoints"}, "ok": true}
